If a patient has an opioid-misuse and has a pain and does not have an opioid-use-disorder and there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician reassesses the pain and ensures a pain-management-therapy-optimization for the patient and discusses a current-dosage-opioid-continuation with the patient and carefully weighs a benefit against a risk for the current-dosage-opioid-continuation.
An opioid-misuse-without-opioid-use-disorder-example is a larger-than-intended-opioid-amount-taking-example.
